  "reasoning": "The payer has issued a CO-18 denial indicating the claim was already adjudicated and paid, which means the payer's records show the obligation is satisfied and resubmission is prohibited. Since the payer considers the claim paid, the remaining open balance on our ledger represents the patient's contractual responsibility (the deductible) that must be collected directly from the patient. Biling the patient is the only action that properly progresses the collection of the allowed amount without violating the payer's duplicate claim rules.",
